  "title": "CXLMC: Model Checking CXL Shared Memory Programs",
  "abstract": "Compute Express Link (CXL) shared memory is an emerging industry standard that will allow for cache coherent sharing of remote memory between many machines. Memory devices will contain large amounts of DRAM that can be shared by many machines in a CXL cluster. This will enable software running on clusters of computers to use shared memory to communicate more efficiently and to share important data between these machines.",
